From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:10:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A backdrop drawn on the GPU beneath the kept scene

`WindowRenderer` gains a backdrop: layers the renderer draws beneath the
scene and animates on its own clock (`set_backdrop`, `backdrop_frame_due`,
`render_backdrop`, `backdrop_frames`). Renderers that can't draw one keep
the defaults, which draw the scene alone.

vello_hybrid keeps the scene in its intermediate texture (drawn over a
transparent background while a backdrop is set) and presents every frame
through one full-surface WGSL pass that draws the base colour and the
layers (linear and radial gradients, a grid, images, embedder WGSL
functions) and composes the scene over them. A frame of the backdrop
alone writes the layers' offsets and records that pass: no scene is
built, encoded or rasterised. Embedder shaders are compiled into the pass
inside a validation error scope (a failing one isn't drawn); their layers
are drawn into a texture of their own only when the backdrop moves or
changes, and timed with timestamp queries where the adapter has them, so a
shader over its budget stops moving.

wgpu_context's SurfaceRenderer can present a frame the embedder draws
straight onto the surface (`present_with`).
